{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/388218-question-about-starting-transmutations-allocation","id":388218,"title":"Question about Starting Transmutations Allocation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-01T03:05:28-08:00","id":388218,"title":"Question about Starting Transmutations Allocation","content":"I had always thought the starting transmutations for a promethean were rather self-explanatory. You get three dots, you can pick three 1dot powers, or a 2dot and a 1dot power or a single 3dot power. (with the caveat that at least one of these transmutations are from your refinement and that you also follow any prerequisites.) I thought this was pretty clear when the example of character creation (on p 90) has the example player choose Mesmerism's Firebringer (a 2dot) and Deception's Color of Man (1dot), totaling 3 dots.<br /> <br /> Now admittedly, this is different than other templates and how they choose their powers (such as vampires, for instance) but I never saw this as a flaw or anything (Promethean's get a lot of cool) just that they were different.<br /> <br /> I have a player in a newly forming chronicle that is arguing that I'm incorrect in the way Prometheans choose their transmutations. She is saying that the example player must use two dots for Mesmerism's Firebringer simply because he does not already have a 1dot transmutation from Mesmerism and that is the penalty he must pay (since Prometheans can buy transmutations &quot;out of order&quot; with experience, pre-GMC, of course). I countered by asking her to bring me some text that supports her claims, but said that while she diligently scours sourcebooks, I would place a query on the forums.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, Promethean's choose their starting powers in a very strange manner when compared to all the other templates. So I'm not saying that I'm right and she's wrong. But the text <i>does</i> seem to support my claim and she seems to be basing her claims mostly on assumptions.<br /> <br /> So who is correct? Or are we both wrong? How do you choose your starting transmutations?<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T03:35:07-08:00","id":388253,"title":"","content":"Your understanding is what I always took away from the book; you get three dots <i>worth</i> of Transmutations, and you have to end up with at least one affinity Transmutation for your Refinement. I'm not sure I understand what your player's argument is; could you rephrase your description of her argument?<br /> <br /> Glancing at the section on choosing Transmutations in character creation, I see that it mentions that some Transmutations can be skipped to directly, while a few have other, lower-dot Transmutations as prerequisites. Perhaps she's conflating this passage with the increased experience costs for purchasing a Transmutation and 'skipping' a dot level? Firebringer doesn't have any prerequisite Transmutations, though, and Promethean follows the general nWoD trend of not distinguishing the costs of 'favored' and 'unfavored' powers purchased with chargen dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T04:38:10-08:00","id":388317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/388218-question-about-starting-transmutations-allocation?p=388253#post388253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Perhaps she's conflating this passage with the increased experience costs for purchasing a Transmutation and 'skipping' a dot level?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly her argument. She is saying that since Prometheans can &quot;skip&quot; levels (i.e. can purchase a 2nd dot Mesmerism transmutation without any other Mesmerism powers at all) when buying with <u>XP</u> and simply pay more <u>experience</u>, that is what the example is doing, except with his starting <u>dots</u>. So basically, by her argument, if the example player were not a moron he <i>could</i> have bought Mesmerism's Fixed stare (for his first dot), <i>then</i> Mesmerism's Firebringer (for his second dot, now not costing extra due to his &quot;skipping&quot;) and finally Deception's Color of Man (for his final dot).<br /> <br /> I, frankly, do not see where she's coming up with this at all. To me it seems rather clear. And as of yet, she cannot find a single piece of <i>text</i> that supports her, simply arguments based on assumptions and applications of other rules to this situation. But I was not going to declare that I was right without at least asking around. I have, after all, been wrong or missed text in the past.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T11:34:39-08:00","id":388663,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it says three dots <i>worth.</i> There's no penalty for starting with Transmutations; the penalty is for buying them with Experience, which you're not doing at character gen. You're getting three dots <i>worth</i>. She is incorrect in her assumption.<br /> Tangentially, I usually let my players pick three 1-2 dot Transmutations flat-out, since they're so variable is use, but that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}